WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.541
Apple removed a

00:00:01.352 --> 00:00:02.873
nine-year-old open-source

00:00:02.685 --> 00:00:03.180
app.

00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:05.553
FSNotes an open-source

00:00:05.365 --> 00:00:06.414
note-taking app

00:00:06.568 --> 00:00:07.664
was removed from

00:00:07.499 --> 00:00:08.536
Apple's EU App

00:00:08.348 --> 00:00:09.669
Stores after nine

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.635
years on sale

00:00:11.158 --> 00:00:12.325
Its developer has

00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:12.915
written up what

00:00:12.726 --> 00:00:13.504
happened in a

00:00:13.316 --> 00:00:14.507
public discussion on

00:00:14.318 --> 00:00:14.978
GitHub

00:00:15.132 --> 00:00:15.674
and how the

00:00:15.486 --> 00:00:17.101
removal unfolded after

00:00:16.913 --> 00:00:18.021
nearly a decade

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:18.634
in the store

00:00:19.166 --> 00:00:20.510
For indie developers

00:00:20.451 --> 00:00:20.946
it is a

00:00:20.758 --> 00:00:22.137
sharp reminder that

00:00:22.079 --> 00:00:23.281
even a long-standing

00:00:23.093 --> 00:00:24.307
app can disappear

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:24.908
from the store

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.404
overnight

00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:26.842
for anyone shipping

00:00:26.654 --> 00:00:27.833
software on someone

00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:28.835
else's platform

00:00:29.358 --> 00:00:30.372
Full story on

00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:31.079
the dashboard
